# TypeScript

## Do

- Keep **`tsc -b`** passing; align new code with settings in **`tsconfig.app.json`**.
- Use **`interface`** for object shapes; **`type`** for unions, intersections, and utilities.
- Prefer **`unknown`** at external boundaries, then narrow with type guards.
- Add explicit **return types** on exported hooks and public service functions when it improves clarity.
- Editor domain types: prefer **`src/features/editor/core/doc/types.ts`** and related modules as the source of truth for nodes/pages — avoid duplicate “shadow” models.

## Don't

- Avoid **`any`**; if unavoidable, add a one-line comment why.
- Avoid **`as` casts** on IndexedDB/API payloads without validation or a documented invariant.
- Avoid `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` without a short justification.

## Security

- Follow **`000-core.mdc`**. Never assume JSON/IDB blobs match types without migration/normalization (see **`migrate.ts`** patterns in editor).
